"""GCM155: Chip multilayer ceramic capacitors, X7R (R7) and C0G (5C), 1005M (0402), AEC-Q200 (GCM series).
GENERATED from component.toml by `python3 -m lib.zen`; do not edit. Source of truth: component.toml and
calc.py (numbers, cites, equations). DS: , 01A (2026-04).
Checks are DC steady-state on the voltages each instance declares. They do not cover transients, overshoot,
hot-plug ringing or load dump. A checked net with no declared voltage reports UNVERIFIED (a warning).
Analysis (worst case, tables, plots) is done in Python: see README.md and calc.py."""

load("@stdlib/units.zen", "Capacitance", "Temperature", "Voltage")

# UNCHECKED: rated_v_ds [parts GCM155R71H104KE02]: Rated voltage (DC) (DS p.2, Rated Value, Rated Voltage (DC 50V)); the generated rated_voltage check applies the catalog rated voltage of the selected part; this per-part row duplicates it (owner: module)
# UNCHECKED: self_heating [parts GCM155R71H104KE02]: Self-heating of the capacitor body (AC or pulse load) (DS p.14, Rating 4. Type of Applied Voltage and Self-heating Temperature); depends on AC/pulse current, not a DC net voltage; owner: module
# UNCHECKED: ac_peak [parts GCM155R71H104KE02]: AC or pulse voltage: peak-to-peak (and zero-to-peak with DC) within the rated DC voltage (DS p.13, Rating 3. Applied Voltage, 1-1 (1)); AC/pulse waveform is not modelled by the DC net-voltage check; owner: module
